1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Imagine painting a
cave wall by firelight,

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:07,076
36,000 years ago.
France's story starts there.

3
00:00:07,116 --> 00:00:09,296
In the Chauvet cave,
early artists paint

4
00:00:09,336 --> 00:00:11,956
lions, horses and a rhino.

5
00:00:11,996 --> 00:00:16,456
In 52 BC, Julius Caesar
defeats the Gauls at Alesia,

6
00:00:16,496 --> 00:00:18,500
and Gaul becomes Roman.

7
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:20,440
In the year 800, Charlemagne

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,931
is crowned emperor
of the West.

9
00:00:22,971 --> 00:00:25,671
In 1429, teenage Joan of Arc

10
00:00:25,711 --> 00:00:28,006
frees the city of Orléans.

11
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:30,146
In 1682, Louis XIV

12
00:00:30,186 --> 00:00:33,907
moves his court
to Versailles.

13
00:00:33,947 --> 00:00:37,247
In 1789, Parisians
storm the Bastille,

14
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:39,961
and the French
Revolution begins.

15
00:00:40,001 --> 00:00:43,861
In 1889, the Eiffel
Tower rises over Paris,

16
00:00:43,901 --> 00:00:46,181
the tallest
structure on Earth.

17
00:00:46,221 --> 00:00:49,321
Today, nearly 69 million
people call France home,

18
00:00:49,361 --> 00:00:52,449
the most visited
country in the world.

19
00:00:52,489 --> 00:00:56,270
Which print is your
favourite? Tell us below.

